      "spear_ef": "100",
      "species": "ELEMENTAL",
      "sprite_battle": "https://assets.forge-vtt.com/610d918102e7ac281373ffcb/Beastiary/Obsidrax_Standard.png",
      "sprite_standard": "https://assets.forge-vtt.com/610d918102e7ac281373ffcb/Beastiary/Obsidrax_Standard.png",
      "steal_percentage_table": {},
      "stealable_loot": {},
      "study_text": "<p>Volcanic glass given a spine. Lightning finds no purchase on it — the storm simply <strong>earths</strong> through the creature and out again, and whatever it is pointed at wears the charge next. The dust it breathes turns flesh to <strong>stone</strong>, which is no mercy: stone only makes the ground answer twice as hard. Thermal shock is the old quarryman's trick — <strong>ice</strong> opens it along the grain.</p>",
